A||||3||Phantom Rage||Another Big Fish Story
Z||000000||Phantom Rage||09-03-99||12:22 PM||||Hello fellow Fieroans, I just go in a race with 3 Mustangs and won.  I know this sounds doubtful, especially since I only have an Iron Duck (88, 5-speed, DIS, but slightly modified.  My best 0 to 60 time is a SLOWWWWW 9.8 sec.  So what gives?  I know some of you will say, they weren’t really racing, that may be true.  Please keep in mind that this is ONLY MY OPINION.  They weren’t new mustangs; they were the previous style.  I figure they must have been 6cyl automatics, yet I bet according to magazines they would still have a better 0-60 time than I.  I really only got into a race with one of them.  This guy was really riding my bumper, So I drooped second.  He hung with me until I shifted into 3rd that’s when I started to slowly pull away.  By forth gear at 4 grand, I had a good 6 car lengths on this guy, so I let off, and of coarse he stayed on it and went flying by.  This is when I looked into the rear view mirror and noticed two more mustangs trying to play catch up and they did, and passed me up.  I couldn't help it, and got on it again.  I passed the two whom just passed me, and caught back up with the first mustang.  I eased off when I got next to the first guy again.  I know he wasn't expecting me to pull up to him again, so to make it things fair I waited till he got on it.  Once again I pulled from him, but this time a bit faster.  5 car lengths ahead I eased off again, but this time for good.  Those guys wouldn’t even pull up next to me now; I was now only doing 50mph. (Speed limit of area)  <br>   I know a whole lot of you guys don't condone racing, especially in public streets.  I will make no excuses, what I did was very dangerous to others and me.  I am 26 years old now, and for the most part I drive 99% slower and safer than, just a few years ago, but every now and then my blood boils and I get the need to prove how big my ego is.  Seems about that time for a speeding ticket.  <br>              P.S. I know I shouldn't brag over v6 mustangs (probably automatic), but when everyone and their grandma rags on 4cyl Fieros, I think you guys get the picture.<br>A) Sorry if this thread gets any angry <br>B) Please don't debate, I'm not going to argue back. <IMG SRC="/ubb/smile.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15><br>
Z||000001||batboy||09-03-99||06:56 PM||||It's hard to be proud and ashamed both, huh?<p>Well, I got into a "race" today with a woman in a Plymouth mini-van. I was driving my "new" 85 GT with a 2.8 and a 4 speed. At a stop light, this lady revs it up and grins at me. I grin back, not thinking anything about it. When the light turned green, she's off the line with the mini-van floored. She even chirped the tires. Kind of caught me off guard. I got over my initial shock, ran through the gears, and finally pass her, but that damn mini-van had more power than I expected and it wasn't an easy win either. Of course, she had me off the line which gave her a great advantage. Watch out for those 30 something housewives, they're hell on wheels.
Z||000002||Patrick||09-03-99||08:07 PM||||<br>So batboy, what happened at the next light? <IMG SRC="/ubb/smile.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15><p>
Z||000003||batboy||09-03-99||11:51 PM||||Well, this was a 4 lane road heading out into the country, so no more traffic lights, She turned onto a side road after about a mile.
